          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A
            %em Lie algebroid
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+categorification"} many object version
            of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+space"} infinitesimal
            approximation to a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoid"} Lie groupoid
          %p There are various equivalent definitions:
          %h3#in_terms_of_vector_bundles_with_anchor In terms of vector bundles with anchor
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_in_terms_of_vector_bundles_with_anchor_map Definition in terms of vector bundles with anchor map
            %p
              A Lie algebroid over a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi E
                          %mo →
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \to X
              %li
                %p
                  equipped with a Lie brackets
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mo ⋅
                        %mo ,
                        %mo ⋅
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo :
                        %mi Γ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi Γ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mi Γ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\cdot,\cdot] : \Gamma(E)\otimes \Gamma(E) \to \Gamma(E)
                  (over the ground field) on its space of sections;
              %li
                %p
                  a morphism of vector bundles
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ρ
                          %mo :
                          %mi E
                          %mo →
                          %mi TX
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho : E \to TX
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi ρ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi ξ
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ζ
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mrow
                              %mi Γ
                              %mi E
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi ρ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi ξ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ρ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi ζ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mrow
                              %mi Γ
                              %mi TX
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\rho)([\xi,\zeta]_{\Gamma E}) = [\rho(\xi),\rho(\zeta)]_{\Gamma TX}
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yvette+Kosmann-Schwarzbach"} Yvette Kosmann-Schwarzbach
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Poisson-Nijenhuis structures
              %li
                %p
                  such that the
                  %em Leibniz rule
                  holds: for all
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Y
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Γ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X, Y \in \Gamma(E)
                  and all
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo ∈
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mn ∞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \in C^\infty(X)
                  we have
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi f
                        %mo ⋅
                        %mi Y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo =
                        %mi f
                        %mo ⋅
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo +
                        %mi ρ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⋅
                        %mi Y
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        [X, f \cdot Y] = f\cdot [X,Y] + \rho(X)(f) \cdot Y
                        \\,.
          %h3#the_cealgebra_of_a_vector_bundle_with_anchor The CE-algebra of a vector bundle with anchor
          %p
            Given this data of a vector bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \to X
            with anchor map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
            as above, one obtains the structure of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebra
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exterior+algebra"} exterior algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mo ∧
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo •
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \wedge^\bullet_{C^\infty(X)} \Gamma(E)^*
            of smooth sections of the dual bundle by the formula
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Shuff
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi sgn
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Shuff
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi sign
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (d\omega)(e_0, \cdots, e_n)
                  \=
                  \\sum_{\sigma \in Shuff(1,n)} sgn(\sigma) \rho(e_{\sigma(0)})(\omega(e_{\sigma(1)}, \cdots, e_{\sigma(n)}))
                  +
                  \\sum_{\sigma \in Shuff(2,n-1)} sign(\sigma)
                  \\omega([e_{\sigma(0)},e_{\sigma(1)}],e_{\sigma(2)}, \cdots, e_{\sigma(n)} )
                  \\,,
          %p
            for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                  %mo ∈
                  %msubsup
                    %mo ∧
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi n
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega \in \wedge^n_{C^\infty(X)} \Gamma(E)^*
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mi i
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (e_i \in \Gamma(E))
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Shuff
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi p
                  %mo ,
                  %mi q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Shuff(p,q)
            denotes the set of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo ,
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p,q)
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shuffle"} shuffle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi sgn
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sgn(\sigma)
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/signature"} signature
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∈
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo ±
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \in \{\pm 1\}
            of the corresponding
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutation"} permutation
          %p
            More details on this are at
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
          %p
            Conversely, one finds that every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semi-free+dga"} semi-free dga
            finitely generated in degree 1 over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(X)
            arises this way, so that one may turn this around:
          %h3#semifree_dgalgebras Semi-free dg-algebras
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_in_terms_of_chevalleyeilenberg_algebra Definition in terms of Chevalley–Eilenberg algebra
            %p
              A Lie algebroid over a manifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a vector bundle
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \to X
              equipped with a degree +1 derivation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
              on the free (over
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(X)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mn ∞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo •
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \wedge^\bullet_{C^\infty(X)} \Gamma(E)^*
              (where the dual is over
              = succeed ")," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi d
                        %mn 2
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d^2 = 0
          %p
            This is for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma(E)
            satisfying suitable finiteness conditions. In general, as the masters well knew, the correct definition is the algebra of alternating multilinear functions from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma(E)
            to the ground field, assumed of characteristic 0. This can also be phrased in terms of linear maps from the corresponding coalgebra cogenerated by
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma(E)
          %p The differential graded-commutative algebra
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CE
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mo ∧
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo •
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo *
                  %mo ,
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  CE(\mathfrak{g})
                  \:=
                  (\wedge^\bullet_{C^\infty(X)} \Gamma(E)^*, d)
          %p
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
            of the Lie algebroid (in that for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo =
                  %mi pt
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = pt
            it reduces to the ordinary Chevally–Eilenberg algebra for Lie algebras).
          %p In the existing literature this is often addressed just as “the complex that computes Lie algebroid cohomology”.
          %p
            It is helpful to compare this definition to the general definition of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+infinity-algebroid"} Lie ∞-algebroids
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertical+categorification"} vertical categorification
            of Lie algebras and Lie algebroids.
          %h3#lierinehart_algebras Lie-Rinehart algebras
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_in_terms_of_commutative_lierinehart_pairs Definition in terms of commutative Lie–Rinehart pairs
            %p
              A Lie algebroid over the manifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  a Lie algebra
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝔤
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              %li
                %p
                  the structure of a Lie module over
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔤
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
                  on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mn ∞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(X)
                  (i.e. an action of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔤
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
                  on
                  = succeed ");" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %li
                %p
                  the structure of a
                  = succeed "-module" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi C
                            %mn ∞
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(X)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔤
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
                  (in fact: such that
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔤
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
                  is a finitely generated projective module);
              %li
                %p
                  such that the two actions satisfy two compatibility conditions which are modeled on the standard relations obtained by setting
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝔤
                          %mo =
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi T
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g} = \Gamma(T X)
          %p
            This is the special case of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie-Rinehart+pair"} Lie-Rinehart pair
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,\mathfrak{g})
            where the associative algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is of the form
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(X)
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                A
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
                is a Lie algebroid over a point,
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo =
                        %mi pt
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = pt
            %li
              %p
                The
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+Lie+algebroid"} tangent Lie algebroid
                is
              %ol
                %li
                  %p
                    in the vector bundle definition given by
                    = succeed "," do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi E
                            %mo =
                            %mi T
                            %mi X
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E = T X
                    = succeed ";" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi ρ
                            %mo =
                            %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Id
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho = \mathrm{Id}
                %li
                  %p
                    in the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
                    definition:
                    = succeed ";" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} CE
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi T
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi Ω
                              %mo •
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi d
                              %mi deRham
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{CE}(T X) = (\Omega^\bullet(X), d_{deRham})
            %li
              %p
                An
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+Lie+algebroid"} action Lie algebroid
                is the Lie version of an
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+groupoid"} action groupoid
            %li
              %p
                %strong Bundles of Lie algebras
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \to X
                with fiber
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔤
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
                are Lie algebroids with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ρ
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho = 0
                and fiberwise bracket. In particular, for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                a Lie group with Lie algebra
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔤
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to X
                a
                = succeed "-principal" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                %em adjoint bundle
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ad
                      %mi P
                      %mo :
                      %mo =
                      %mi P
                      %msub
                        %mo ×
                        %mi G
                      %mi 𝔤
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ad P := P \times_G \mathfrak{g}
                (where
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔤
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
                is associated using the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+representation"} adjoint representation
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                on its Lie algebra) is a bundle of Lie algebras.
            %li
              %p
                Lie algebroids with injective anchor maps are equivalently
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integrable+distributions"} integrable distributions
                in the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent bundle
                of their base manifold and hence are equivalently
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foliations"} foliations
                of their base manifold.
            %li
              %p
                The
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Atiyah+Lie+algebroid"} Atiyah Lie algebroid
                is the Lie algebroid of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Atiyah+Lie+groupoid"} Atiyah Lie groupoid
                of a principal bundle: for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                a Lie group and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to X
                a
                = succeed "-principal" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi At
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mo =
                      %mi T
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} At(P):= T P/G
                naturally inherits the structure of a Lie algebroid. Moreover, it fits into a short exact sequence of Lie algebroids over
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo →
                      %mi ad
                      %mi P
                      %mo →
                      %mi At
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi T
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      0 \to ad P \to At(P) \to T X \to 0
              %p
                known as the
                = succeed "." do
                  %strong Atiyah sequence
            %li
              %p
                The
                %strong vertical tangent Lie algebroid
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mi vert
                      %mi Y
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi T
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_{vert}Y \hookrightarrow T Y
                of a smooth map
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi π
                      %mo :
                      %mi Y
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi : Y \to X
                of manifolds is the sub-Lie algebroid of the tangent Lie algebroid
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T Y
                defined as follows:
              %ol
                %li
                  %p
                    In the vector bundle perspective
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi E
                          %mo =
                          %mi ker
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi π
                            %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E = ker(\pi_*)
                    is the kernel bundle of the map
                    = succeed "." do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi π
                              %mo *
                            %mo :
                            %mi T
                            %mi Y
                            %mo →
                            %mi T
                            %mi X
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_* : T Y \to T X
                %li
                  %p
                    In the dual picture we have
                    = succeed "," do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi CE
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi T
                              %mi vert
                            %mi Y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo =
                            %msubsup
                              %mi Ω
                              %mi vert
                              %mo •
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CE(T_{vert}Y) = \Omega^\bullet_{vert}(Y)
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+infinity-algebroid"} qDGCA
                    of
                    = succeed "." do
                      %strong vertical differential forms
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi Ω
                            %mo •
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^\bullet(Y)
                    by the ideal of those forms which vanish when restricted in all arguments to
                    = succeed "." do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi ker
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi π
                              %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ker(\pi_*)
            %li
              %p
                Each
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+manifold"} Poisson manifold
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi π
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\pi)
                defines and is defined by a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+Lie+algebroid"} Poisson Lie algebroid
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi T
                          %mo *
                        %mi X
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mi π
                        %mi t
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T^* X \stackrel{\pi}{\to} t X
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-symplectic+manifold"} n-symplectic manifold
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E\to X
                is a Lie algebroid with bracket
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [,]
                and anchor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ρ
                      %mo :
                      %mi E
                      %mo →
                      %mi TX
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho:E\to TX
                then it induces a Lie algebroid structure on the
                = succeed "-th" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jet+bundle"} jet
                bundle
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi j
                          %mi k
                        %mi E
                        %mo →
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j^k E\to X
                = succeed "." do
                  %strong jet Lie algebroid
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi Γ
                        %mi X
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s\in\Gamma_X E
                then call by
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi j
                        %mi k
                      %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j^k s
                the induced section in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Γ
                          %mi X
                        %msup
                          %mi j
                          %mi k
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma_X j^k E
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi j
                        %mi k
                      %mi E
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j^k E\to X
                such that the following two properties hold:
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi j
                        %mi k
                      %mi s
                      %mo ,
                      %msup
                        %mi j
                        %mi k
                      %mi t
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo =
                      %msup
                        %mi j
                        %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi s
                      %mo ,
                      %mi t
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [j^k s, j^k t] = j^k [s,t]
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ρ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi j
                        %mi k
                      %mi s
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi ρ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi s
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho(j^k s) = \rho(s)
                for all
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo ,
                      %mi t
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi Γ
                        %mi X
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s,t\in\Gamma_X E
                (see
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.ist.utl.pt/~rfern/Meus-papers/HTML/jets.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BRST+complex"} BRST complex
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
                of a Lie algebroid which corresponds to the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+groupoid"} action groupoid
                of a Lie group acting on a space.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#lie_theory_2 Lie theory
          %p
            The extent to which Lie algebroids are to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoid"} Lie groupoids
            as Lie algebras are to Lie groups is the content of general
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+theory"} Lie theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie%27s+three+theorems"} Lie's theorems
            have been generalized to Lie algebroids.
          %h3#poisson_geometry Poisson geometry
          %p
            The fiberwise linear dual of a Lie algebroid (regarded as a vector bundle) is naturally a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+manifold"} Poisson manifold
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie-Poisson+structure"} Lie-Poisson structure
