          %h2#references References
          %p The concept of Lie algebroid was introduced in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean+Pradines"}> Jean Pradines
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Théorie de Lie pour les groupoïdes différentiables. Calcul différenetiel dans la catégorie des groupoïdes infinitésimaux
              %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=0216409"} MR0216409
          %p In algebra, a generalization of Lie algebroid, the Lie pseudoalgebra or Lie-Rinehart algebra/pair has been introduced more than a dozen of times under various names starting in early 1950-s. Atiyah’s construction of Atiyah sequence is published in 1957 and Rinehart’s paper in 1963.
          %p Historically important is also the reference
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Theodore+Courant"}> Theodore Courant
              ,
              %em Tangent Lie algebroid
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.iop.org/EJ/article/0305-4470/27/13/026/ja941326.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+Lie+algebroids"} tangent Lie algebroids
          %p A bijective correspondence between Lie algebroid structures, homological vector fields of degree 1, and odd linear Poisson structures is established in the paper
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A.+Yu.+Vaintrob"}> A. Yu. Vaintrob
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Lie algebroids and homological vector fields
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1070/rm1997v052n02abeh001802"} doi
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/vaintrob.pdf", :title => "PDF"} PDF
          %p Textbook accounts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kirill+Mackenzie"}> Kirill Mackenzie
                ,
                %em General theory of Lie groupoids and Lie algebroids,
                Cambridge University Press, 2005, xxxviii + 501 pages (
                %a{:href => "http://kchmackenzie.staff.shef.ac.uk/gt.html"}> website
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kirill+Mackenzie"}> Kirill Mackenzie
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Lie groupoids and Lie algebroids in differential geometry
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=896907"} MathSciNet
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Janez+Mr%C4%8Dun"}> Janez Mrčun
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"} Ieke Moerdijk
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Introduction to foliations and Lie groupoids
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 91
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Xavier+Bekaert"}> Xavier Bekaert
                ,
                %em Geometric tool kit for higher spin gravity (part II): An introduction to Lie algebroids and their enveloping algebras
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2308.00724"}> arXiv:2308.00724
                \&amp;rbrack;
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (motivated by
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+spin+gauge+theory"} higher spin gauge theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eckhard+Meinrenken"}> Eckhard Meinrenken
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Lie Algebroids
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Encyclopedia+of+Mathematical+Physics+2nd+ed"} Encyclopedia of Mathematical Physics 2nd ed
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2401.03034"} arXiv:2401.03034
          %p For an infinite-dimensional version used in stochastic analysis see
          %ul
            %li
              Rémi Léandre,
              = succeed "," do
                %em A Lie algebroid on the Wiener space
              %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=2594930"} MR2011j:58064
          %p There is also a recent “hom-version”
          %ul
            %li
              Camille Laurent-Gengoux, Joana Teles,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Hom-Lie algebroids
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1211.2263"} arxiv/1211.2263
